thon.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#str"><literal_emphasis>str</literal_emphasis></reference><literal_emphasis>]</literal_emphasis><literal_emphasis>] </literal_emphasis><literal_emphasis>| </literal_emphasis><literal_emphasis>None</literal_emphasis>) – Data to encode and send in the request body.</paragraph>
                                </list_item>
                                <list_item>
                                    <paragraph><literal_strong>headers</literal_strong> (<reference internal="0" reftitle="(in Python v3.15)" refuri="https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.Mapping"><literal_emphasis>Mapping</literal_emphasis></reference><literal_emphasis>[</literal_emphasis><reference internal="0" reftitle="(in Python v3.15)" refuri="https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#str"><literal_emphasis>str</literal_emphasis></reference><literal_emphasis>, </literal_emphasis><reference internal="0" reftitle="(in Python v3.15)" refuri="https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#str"><literal_emphasis>str</literal_emphasis></reference><literal_emphasis>] </literal_emphasis><literal_emphasis>| </literal_emphasis><literal_emphasis>None</literal_emphasis>) – Dictionary of custom headers to send, such as User-Agent,
